/*
Mental trigger

“Range with one missing value → XOR indices and elements.”

Time complexity

O(n)

Space complexity

O(1)

Simple intuition

Numbers should be 0..n, but one is missing

XOR has the canceling property: a ^ a = 0

XOR all:

every index i

every value nums[i]

All matching pairs cancel out

The only number that doesn’t get canceled is the missing one

Starting with val = n accounts for the last number (n) which has no index.
*/
class Solution {
    public int missingNumber(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int val = n;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            val ^= i ^ nums[i];
        }
        return val;
    }
}
